1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:01,630
If your knee replacement still

2
00:00:01,630 --> 00:00:03,050
hurts and the X-ray keeps

3
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,700
coming back fine, don't accept that.

4
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:06,660
I've been an operating

5
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,460
room nurse for thirty years.

6
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:09,700
Standing still on a hard

7
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,160
floor for hours, case after case.

8
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:12,810
I had my right

9
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:14,600
knee replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,540
It has hurt every day since.

11
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,790
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,200
I know what that felt like,

13
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,260
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,450
This is different.

15
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:23,170
Tight.

16
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:23,940
Full.

17
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,760
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,500
the joint that never loosens.

19
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:27,650
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,100
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:30,180
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:31,820
At six weeks it was swelling,

23
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:33,430
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:35,960
At three months, give it six.

25
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:37,120
At six months, some

26
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,550
knees take a full year.

27
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:41,260
At a year, eighteen months isn't unusual.

28
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:42,640
And I didn't just wait.

29
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,860
We went down the list.

30
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,390
More physical therapy.

31
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:46,610
Every session,

32
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,840
every exercise at home.

33
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,930
I got stronger.

34
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:51,440
The tightness never moved.

35
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,790
The pain pills helped,

36
00:00:52,790 --> 00:00:54,160
and that was the problem.

37
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:56,130
I'm already on enough every morning,

38
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:57,290
and nobody could tell me

39
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:58,610
when I'd get to stop.

40
00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:00,080
Then a nerve block.

41
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,830
Then talk of burning the nerve.

42
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,670
And after that, a second

43
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:04,940
operation to go back

44
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,370
in and do it over.

45
00:01:06,370 --> 00:01:07,410
I said no.

46
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:08,750
Every morning I stepped out

47
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:09,780
of bed and my knee

48
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:10,650
felt like a band

49
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:12,470
was wrapped around it, tightening

50
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:14,580
every inch I tried to straighten.

51
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:15,990
Every morning I took something

52
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:17,840
for it and went to my shift.

53
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:19,230
Couldn't do the stairs,

54
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,410
couldn't stand at the counter

55
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,960
long enough to finish dinner,

56
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,420
couldn't sit through my granddaughter's

57
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:25,970
game without shifting every two minutes.

58
00:01:25,970 --> 00:01:27,330
In a long surgery,

59
00:01:27,330 --> 00:01:28,550
I'd be rocking from foot

60
00:01:28,550 --> 00:01:29,990
to foot just to make

61
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:31,060
it to the end.

62
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:32,850
It woke me at night,

63
00:01:32,850 --> 00:01:34,720
and it turned ordinary things,

64
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,720
like getting in the car

65
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,960
after a shift or up

66
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,290
off the couch, into a decision.

67
00:01:39,290 --> 00:01:40,420
After a long and serious

68
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:41,820
talk with my husband,

69
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:43,690
I went back in one more time.

70
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:44,690
That was the fourth set

71
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:46,230
of X-rays on this knee.

72
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:47,770
And like the three before it,

73
00:01:47,770 --> 00:01:50,440
the answer was everything looks great.

74
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:53,600
No loosening, no infection, nothing wrong.

75
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:54,900
Only this time there

76
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:56,350
was no new number.

77
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,390
Nobody said give it another six months.

78
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:01,140
There was nothing left to give it.

79
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:02,060
I sat in the parking

80
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:03,300
lot for a while.

81
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,910
Okay, I thought.

82
00:02:04,910 --> 00:02:06,280
Then explain this.

83
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,430
Anyway,

84
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:08,740
a couple of months back,

85
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,320
I hit my breaking point.

86
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:12,450
It was around 2:30 in the morning.

87
00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:13,440
Everyone in the house

88
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,300
was asleep and I was downstairs

89
00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:16,560
in the recliner with my leg

90
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,900
up, trying to find

91
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,190
any angle where it didn't

92
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:20,560
feel like something was wrapped

93
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,540
around my knee and tightening.

94
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:24,450
I had to scrub in at seven.

95
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:27,130
My husband didn't know I'd come downstairs.

96
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:29,970
By then I'd stopped telling him.

97
00:02:29,970 --> 00:02:31,100
And I just thought,

98
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,910
is this really my life now?

99
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,480
I can't live like this.

100
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,940
Thirty years on my feet,

101
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:37,720
and I couldn't trust my own knee.

102
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,570
So I made myself a promise.

103
00:02:39,570 --> 00:02:40,380
I wouldn't go a day

104
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:42,110
without looking for an answer.

105
00:02:42,110 --> 00:02:43,290
And when I found one,

106
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:44,390
I'd share it with everyone

107
00:02:44,390 --> 00:02:45,860
going through the same thing.

108
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,080
So I got my laptop

109
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:48,280
out and went looking.

110
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:49,440
Not for a product.

111
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,920
For an explanation.

112
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:52,740
Mayo Clinic forums,

113
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:54,950
the knee replacement group on Facebook,

114
00:02:54,950 --> 00:02:57,820
doctor videos, medical animations.

115
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,230
And that's when I found a video

116
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:01,080
from a physical therapist named Dr.

117
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,510
Steven Salinger,

118
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:04,550
whose own wife had

119
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:06,520
been through exactly this.

120
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,470
But before I say anything else,

121
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:10,150
I want to be straight with you.

122
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:12,360
You've already had something work fast.

123
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,230
The ice.

124
00:03:13,230 --> 00:03:14,960
The first week of a new pill.

125
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,750
The good day after a session.

126
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,360
Then it wore off.

127
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,320
That's the part nobody warns you about.

128
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:22,370
Fast relief isn't relief.

129
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:23,430
It's a preview.

130
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:25,030
So I'm not going

131
00:03:25,030 --> 00:03:26,620
to tell you this works fast.

132
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:27,530
It doesn't.

133
00:03:27,530 --> 00:03:29,160
But if you're willing to be patient,

134
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:29,990
and to look at what's

135
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:31,080
going on around your new

136
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,850
knee instead of inside it,

137
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:33,620
there is a real

138
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,190
reason it still hurts.

139
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,950
And something you can do about it.

140
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,200
Let me explain what he said,

141
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,040
because this is what

142
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,720
changed everything for me.

143
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,770
He started with the basics.

144
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:45,110
A knee replacement takes

145
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:46,660
out the worn joint surfaces

146
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:48,690
and puts in metal and plastic.

147
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:50,190
That's what stops the arthritis

148
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:52,320
pain you had before the operation.

149
00:03:52,320 --> 00:03:54,050
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:55,990
But then he explained something

151
00:03:55,990 --> 00:03:57,600
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,840
He said, think about

153
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,610
a swollen foot inside a shoe.

154
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:02,030
The shoe didn't shrink.

155
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:03,030
Your foot is taking up

156
00:04:03,030 --> 00:04:04,770
more room, so everything feels

157
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:06,990
cramped and tight and squeezed.

158
00:04:06,990 --> 00:04:07,970
Your new knee sits

159
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:09,700
in a limited space with living

160
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,770
tissue packed all around it.

161
00:04:11,770 --> 00:04:12,950
To put that knee in,

162
00:04:12,950 --> 00:04:13,710
the surgeon had

163
00:04:13,710 --> 00:04:15,350
to work through that tissue.

164
00:04:15,350 --> 00:04:18,410
Afterwards it gets inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:20,180
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:21,000
But in some people

167
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,360
that swelling can stay switched

168
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:24,350
on far longer than expected.

169
00:04:24,350 --> 00:04:25,830
And swollen tissue takes up

170
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,920
more room than calm tissue does.

171
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,740
So when you bend,

172
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:32,010
that tissue gets compressed.

173
00:04:32,010 --> 00:04:34,720
When you straighten, it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,760
That's the band.

175
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:38,440
That's the ache that never quite leaves.

176
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,500
And you start being the one

177
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,410
who says, you go ahead.

178
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:42,430
I'll stay here.

179
00:04:42,430 --> 00:04:44,120
And that's exactly why so much

180
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,970
of what I'd tried hadn't worked.

181
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,010
Physical therapy strengthens

182
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:49,790
the muscles around the knee.

183
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,020
Worth doing,

184
00:04:51,020 --> 00:04:51,910
and

185
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:52,950
I'd done it.

186
00:04:52,950 --> 00:04:53,950
It does nothing about

187
00:04:53,950 --> 00:04:55,720
tissue taking up room.

188
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,080
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,390
the nerve carrying the signal.

190
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:02,040
It doesn't touch what's generating it.

191
00:05:02,470 --> 00:05:04,540
But when that irritated tissue finally

192
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:07,100
calms down, it holds less fluid,

193
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,870
and it takes up less room.

194
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:10,550
Less room taken up means

195
00:05:10,550 --> 00:05:13,010
less pressure squeezing the joint.

196
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:15,110
That's what takes the pressure off.

197
00:05:15,110 --> 00:05:16,710
After two years of this,

198
00:05:16,710 --> 00:05:18,330
it finally made sense.

199
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:20,900
The problem was never the new knee.

200
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:22,840
It was the tissue crowded around it.

201
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,450
He calls it the squeeze.

202
00:05:24,450 --> 00:05:26,760
Once you've felt it, that's the word.

203
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:29,380
I'd bought knee sleeves, compression braces,

204
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:31,990
creams, half of Amazon really,

205
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:33,230
and all any of it gave

206
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:34,800
me was an hour.

207
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:35,820
I even looked at going

208
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:37,840
to a clinic for the light therapy.

209
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,810
But at $200 a session

210
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,670
with nothing covered by insurance,

211
00:05:41,670 --> 00:05:43,110
that was a quick no.

212
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,510
Then one night

213
00:05:44,890 --> 00:05:45,930
I went back to that knee

214
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:48,340
replacement group and actually read it.

215
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:50,410
Thousands of people, years out

216
00:05:50,410 --> 00:05:52,790
from surgery, comparing notes on stiffness

217
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,180
and tightness nobody could explain.

218
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:57,130
And no matter how far I scrolled,

219
00:05:57,130 --> 00:05:58,860
the same thing kept coming up.

220
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,950
This one device, and people

221
00:06:00,950 --> 00:06:02,230
saying it was the first

222
00:06:02,230 --> 00:06:03,920
thing that made a difference.

223
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:06,110
And before anyone jumps in thinking,

224
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:08,500
alright, here it comes,

225
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,200
she's selling me something, let

226
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,240
me shut that down right now.

227
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,270
I'm only here because

228
00:06:13,270 --> 00:06:14,470
I made myself a promise

229
00:06:14,470 --> 00:06:15,990
at 2:30 in the morning

230
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:17,020
that if I ever found

231
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,320
something that helped, I'd say so.

232
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:21,620
It's called the KenRelief

233
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:23,250
Red Light Therapy Wrap.

234
00:06:23,790 --> 00:06:26,040
At first glance I didn't buy it.

235
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,040
It looked like the cheap

236
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,380
knee sleeves off Amazon

237
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:29,980
that did nothing for me.

238
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:30,650
But I went to their

239
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:32,580
website anyway, just to see what

240
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:34,000
all the fuss was about.

241
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,490
It's the same red light therapy

242
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:38,680
clinics charge $200 a session for,

243
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:41,390
off machines that cost fifty thousand dollars,

244
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:42,340
in a wrap you plug

245
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:43,740
into the wall at home.

246
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,490
Two hundred and forty lights.

247
00:06:45,490 --> 00:06:47,690
Red at 660 nanometers

248
00:06:47,690 --> 00:06:50,250
and near-infrared at 850,

249
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:52,520
run together for the strongest effect.

250
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:53,920
Four strength levels.

251
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:55,900
A five to thirty minute timer.

252
00:06:55,900 --> 00:06:57,480
Then I saw the guarantee.

253
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,780
Ninety days.

254
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:00,580
Results or your money back,

255
00:07:00,580 --> 00:07:03,110
no questions, no store credit,

256
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:04,860
and you don't even send it back.

257
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:07,320
No physical therapist ever gave me

258
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,160
ninety days to change my mind.

259
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,260
There wasn't much to lose,

260
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:11,640
so I ordered it.

261
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:13,090
Two of them, actually.

262
00:07:13,090 --> 00:07:14,860
Only the right knee was replaced,

263
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:16,730
but you favor the leg that hurts,

264
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:17,940
and I'd done it on every

265
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,500
shift for two years.

266
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:22,050
The left one was carrying the difference.

267
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:23,520
When it came, I strapped

268
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,150
it on expecting nothing,

269
00:07:25,150 --> 00:07:26,280
because I'd been let down

270
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,270
too many times to get excited.

271
00:07:28,270 --> 00:07:29,930
What I felt was warmth.

272
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:31,880
Not a heating pad kind of hot.

273
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:32,830
More like it was coming

274
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,970
from inside the knee

275
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:35,450
and spreading around it.

276
00:07:35,450 --> 00:07:36,680
And that was it.

277
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:38,460
That was the whole experience.

278
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,630
When I took it off,

279
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:42,430
I'll be honest, nothing dramatic had happened.

280
00:07:42,430 --> 00:07:44,280
And after what that video said,

281
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:46,230
that's exactly what I expected.

282
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:47,060
What was different

283
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:47,990
was that for the first

284
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:49,420
time in two years

285
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:50,950
I'd done something for my knee

286
00:07:50,950 --> 00:07:52,190
instead of to it.

287
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:54,230
Twenty minutes, in my own

288
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:55,870
chair, after my shift.

289
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:57,690
No drive, no copay.

290
00:07:57,690 --> 00:07:59,170
They say twenty minutes.

291
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:00,720
I did thirty,

292
